[I] Bash Library for Indolent Programmers

[T] blip (Bash Library for Indolent Programmers) is a shell library
[T] providing functions for many common tasks in Bash scripts, to fill the
[T] gap in reusable Bash code. Scripts source /usr/lib/blip.bash and the
[T] functions are documented in the blip.bash man page.

[U] https://nicolaw.uk/blip

[A] Blip Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

